---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: "Privacy Policy",
  description: "Learn how EduGlossary handles technical data, restricted GA4 measurement, Monetag push advertising, security, and privacy choices.",
};

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: "Home", href: "/" },
  { label: "Privacy Policy", href: "/privacy-policy/" },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Learn how EduGlossary handles technical data, restricted GA4 measurement, Monetag push advertising, security, and privacy choices."
  schema={schema}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: November 12, 2026</em></p>

    <p>
      This policy explains what information EduGlossary (eduglossary.my.id) processes when you
      visit the site, why it is used, and the choices available to you. The site is operated by the
      <a href="/authors/eduglossary-team/">EduGlossary Team</a>. You can reach us at
      <a href="mailto:admin@eduglossary.my.id">admin@eduglossary.my.id</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p>
      EduGlossary has no user accounts, no comments, and no forms that collect personal details.
      We do not ask you for your name or email address to read the site. If you email us, we
      receive the address and the content of your message and use them to respond.
    </p>
    <p>
      When a page loads, your browser may provide technical information such as an IP address,
      browser and device details, referring page, and page path. Our hosting, analytics, and
      advertising providers may process some of this information to deliver their services.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
      EduGlossary no longer uses a cookie-consent banner. Google Consent Mode is configured with
      analytics and advertising storage denied by default. GA4 may therefore receive restricted,
      cookieless measurement signals, but Google Analytics cookies such as <code>_ga</code> and
      <code>_ga_*</code> are not enabled by this configuration. Cloudflare may use strictly
      necessary security technologies. Monetag may use advertising cookies or similar technologies
      as described in its own policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Google tag and Google Analytics 4 (GA4)</strong> help us understand page views
        and on-site search activity. We use a direct Google tag, not Google Tag Manager. Analytics
        and advertising storage remain denied by default through Google Consent Mode, so the
        integration is configured for restricted cookieless measurement. Pagefind search events
        send the event type and query length, not the text entered into the search box. See the
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Monetag</strong> provides Push Notifications advertising. Its tag and service
        worker enable the browser notification opt-in flow. If you grant notification permission,
        your browser may receive advertising notifications even when you are no longer visiting
        this site. You can revoke that permission in your browser or device notification settings.
        Monetag may process technical, browser, advertising, and interaction data under its own
        policies. See the
        <a href="https://monetag.com/privacy/" rel="noopener">Monetag Privacy Policy</a>,
        <a href="https://monetag.com/cookies-policy/" rel="noopener">Cookies Policy</a>, and
        <a href="https://monetag.com/opt-out/" rel="noopener">Opt-Out information</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloudflare</strong> delivers and protects the site through content delivery,
        security, and bot protection. It may use a security cookie such as
        <code>cf_clearance</code>. See the
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <p>
      We use technical information to operate and secure the site, understand which pages and
      search features are useful, and provide advertising through Monetag. We do not sell
      information that directly identifies you.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Manage or delete cookies through your browser settings.</li>
      <li>
        Allow, block, or revoke EduGlossary notification permission through your browser or
        device's site-notification settings. Push notifications stop after permission is revoked.
      </li>
      <li>
        Use the <a href="https://monetag.com/opt-out/" rel="noopener">Monetag opt-out page</a>
        for the advertising preferences covered by that tool. Push notification subscriptions
        must be managed separately through browser notification settings.
      </li>
      <li>
        You may opt out of Google Analytics using the
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights over your personal data, including
        access, correction, or deletion. To make a request, email
        <a href="mailto:admin@eduglossary.my.id">admin@eduglossary.my.id</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      We do not maintain user accounts or site-submitted personal profiles. Emails you send us
      remain in our mailbox as needed to respond and maintain relevant correspondence. Data
      processed by third-party providers is retained according to their own policies and settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      EduGlossary is an educational website for a general audience. Visitors do not need to
      provide personal information to read the site, and we do not knowingly collect personal
      information directly from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal
      information to us, please contact
      <a href="mailto:admin@eduglossary.my.id">admin@eduglossary.my.id</a> so we can review the
      matter and take appropriate steps.
    </p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>
      The site may link to other websites. We are not responsible for their privacy practices.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The date at the top indicates when it
      was last updated. We encourage you to review this page periodically.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy? See our <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page or email
      <a href="mailto:admin@eduglossary.my.id">admin@eduglossary.my.id</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
